A||||10||86GT-FstBk||Quarter Window Help NOW!!||||5||
Z||000000||86GT-FstBk||09-15-2000||04:45 PM||||I'm trying to reinstall my pass. side quarter window.  What kind of tape will work to hold this baby on.  TIA, Brian||||reg||5
Z||000001||stsmithgt||09-15-2000||05:13 PM||||I heard that 3M makes a heavy duty double-stick tape that does the job well.  I'm waiting on some windows to come in and I'll have to investivgate this further also.  Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000002||PJ||09-15-2000||07:33 PM||||3M makes a two-sided, white foam tape marketed for installing auto trim. It has a red release liner. It's available at Auto Paint & Body supply shops. There is also a version 3M sells through Home Depots and the like with a green liner. I could be wrong but I think they're identical. I've used both versions with one caveat. The tapes don't work all that well. They eventually come loose at some points due to flex in the body panels and the not too great fit to begin with (they used to fly off ($$$!) when I got the car sideways or spun at high speeds). I once tried gluing them in with windshield urethane and they cracked ($$$!) due to the flexing. I'm currently using 1/8" home-made lexan panels riveted to the quarter panels. Try doubling up the tape where the gaps occur.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Archie||09-16-2000||09:07 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by PJ:<BR><B> (they used to fly off ($$$!) when I got the car sideways or spun at high speeds).<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR> <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Oh come on...... What are you driving a NASCAR stockcar? Most people that spin at high speed have a lot more to worry about that the side windows blowing out.<P>Give me a break. Let's just say you don't like the 3M tape. Just how fast do you have to get your Fiero going to be able to spin it at a speed high enough that it'll blow the windows out? <P>PJ doesn't stand for Parnelli Jones does it?, If it does, I take it all back..... ;-)<P>Archie||||reg||6
Z||000004||PJ||09-16-2000||11:11 AM||||Archie:<P>SCCA road racing. Only about 80 or 90 mph. Almost creamed a guy in a Miata with one once.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||09-16-2000||11:53 AM||||That should teach those pesky Miata's  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">    <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
Z||000006||My7Fieros||09-16-2000||03:01 PM||||Hey you know this really is a good question (for me at least). Im getting ready to put my quarter windows back on my Formula and Id like to know to. I read somewhere about using that 3M tape..I was going to go get some. I dont want my windows falling off though! <BR>Keep in mind, the Formula is a daily, city driver, not a hotrod. Will this tape work (along the front of the window, along the "pillar" part, where the Pontiac logo is?<BR>I hope so, itll be the only thing holding that side down, the angled part has the "christmas tree" fittings that snap in.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||09-16-2000||03:10 PM||||My7Fieros--Don't use tape to hold any part of the fixture in place.  There are 2 "Christmas trees" in the back and a metal clip in the front.  If you're missing the metal clip, get another one.  Tape alone won't hold it.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Archie||09-16-2000||06:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by PJ:<BR><B>Archie:<P>SCCA road racing. Only about 80 or 90 mph. Almost creamed a guy in a Miata with one once.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hehe there you go. My point is that most of us who get into a 360 degree spin will have a lot more to worry about than the 1/4 windows.<P>the tape seems to work find for me, but I have not driven it backwards at anything more than 70MPH.<P>Archie<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||PJ||09-16-2000||11:40 PM||||Sorry if I didn't make it clear. The tape is the way to go if you don't expect to do 180's. I was bitchin' about the poor fit.<P>Luckily the guy in the Miata was runnin' with the hard top. I guess they call 'em "sail panels'" for a reason. :)<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR>||||reg||1
